From 41c7f3f1ad7114bd2dab6e44d2128e07d2d9c895 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:46:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat: close a programme without hiding it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Close was ambiguous: on the creation form it dismissed the panel, which is
not what closing a programme means. That button is now Cancel, and closing
is a real thing that happens to a programme.

A fourth state, closed: still on the public catalogue, but sign-ups are
over. A cohort that has filled up or already started is not a secret —
people should be able to read what the Lab runs and see that this one has
closed, rather than meet a page that no longer exists. Archived remains
for taking something off the site altogether.

The rules live in @workspace/domain so the catalogue and the enrolment
endpoint cannot disagree; a status nobody planned for falls back to hidden
and closed rather than to accepting sign-ups. Each programme card now
carries the one press that matters — Publish, Close, or Reopen sign-ups —
and every state says in words what it does.

Also: the thumbnail upload now shows the server's actual reason instead of
'try again'.

