From b35b4f504cb9717578cf3de4b60966e4f6831715 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:03:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat: type a facilitator's name, or pick one
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The facilitator box was a dropdown of people who hold accounts, so a guest
speaker who appears for one evening could not be named at all.

It is now a box you can type into, with the account holders offered as you
type. A name that belongs to somebody with an account gives them the class
— their dashboard, the room, attendance, submissions. Anything else is
recorded as a guest: shown to learners, granting nothing, because handing
an account to a one-evening visitor would open fifty learners' work.

Two people of the same name is refused rather than guessed at; the box asks
for an email instead. A session never carries both an account holder and a
typed name, so no page has to choose between two answers.

Adds one database column, so the schema update needs running again.

